1. FREE USE (No License Required)

   Events, venues, or gatherings with up to 1,000 persons may use,
   copy, modify, and distribute the Software free of charge, provided
   that the official OpenSonic application is used.

   Personal, educational, and non-commercial use is always free
   regardless of scale.


2. COMMERCIAL USE (License Required)

   Events exceeding 1,000 persons require a commercial license.

   +-------------------+------------------+-----------------+
   | Tier              | Per-Event        | Annual          |
   +-------------------+------------------+-----------------+
   | S: 1,001 - 5,000  | $299 / event     | $999 / year     |
   | M: 5,001 - 10,000 | $799 / event     | $2,499 / year   |
   | L: 10,001+        | $1,999 / event   | $4,999 / year   |
   +-------------------+------------------+-----------------+

   Annual licenses cover unlimited events within the tier for one year.
   All prices in USD.

   For comparison: Dante requires $41+ per device in hardware licensing
   plus $400-$10,000/year for management software. OpenSonic runs on
   commodity hardware (Raspberry Pi, any Linux/macOS device) with no
   per-device fees.


3. OFFICIAL APPLICATION REQUIREMENT

   Commercial use must run the official, unmodified OpenSonic binary
   distributed at https://github.com/yukihamada/opensonic or through
   official package repositories. Forks and modified builds are
   permitted for development and testing, but production use at
   commercial events requires the official release.


